Cisco Hybrid Networking Lab

Physical Cisco Infrastructure, CML Virtualization, and Secure Remote Access

Project Overview
This project focuses on building a hybrid Cisco networking environment that combines physical network equipment with Cisco Modeling Labs (CML).

The objective is to create a realistic environment for studying enterprise networking, routing protocols, remote administration, VPN technologies, and troubleshooting.

The lab was built using personal networking equipment, a residential fiber connection, and virtual Cisco routers.

Primary technologies:

Cisco IOS
Cisco Modeling Labs (CML)
IKEv2 / IPsec FlexVPN
PKI and certificate-based authentication
SSH remote administration
VLANs and switched virtual interfaces (SVIs)
Static routing
OSPF
NAT traversal
Windows PowerShell and OpenSSH
