Security Considerations
The lab was designed with several security practices in mind:

Certificate-based VPN authentication.
Encrypted IPsec remote-access traffic.
Dedicated management addressing.
No direct public SSH exposure.
Private certificate authority.
Protected certificate private keys.
Split tunneling for lab-specific access.
Removal of unnecessary web management services.
Separation between virtual routing experiments and physical network infrastructure.
The physical equipment runs legacy IOS software, so some compatibility limitations remain.

Future improvements include modernizing cryptographic algorithms where hardware support permits, strengthening management access controls, and implementing certificate revocation procedures.

